# JES cameras and parallax
@scenario tutorial_lesson_40
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/40_jes_camera.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt push_camera]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: A JES camera can travel past layers at different rates. Look at the distant and nearby landmarks while the view moves.
@label lab
> Run the camera demo -> camera
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label camera
[if tutorial_still]
ginger: Reduced motion is enabled. You can read the camera setup in the code panel without playing the moving scene.
[jump compare]
[endif]
# region push_camera
[jes push scripts/scenes/camera.jes label compare]
# endregion
@label compare
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/camera.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt parallax]
ginger: Compare the two landmarks. Change the distant landmark's parallax factor to 1 in camera.jes and reopen the demo.
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_40]
[flag tutorial_done_40]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_8]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Set distant and near to the same factor. What should happen?
> The camera pan stops. -> practice_hint
> Both landmarks shift by the same amount. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: Their relative horizontal displacement should now stay constant during the pan.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: Their relative horizontal displacement should now stay constant during the pan.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the interactive lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Which landmark moves less during the camera pan?
> The distant landmark with factor 0.3. -> correct
> The landmark with factor 1. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The parallax factor scales displacement from camera movement.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The parallax factor scales displacement from camera movement.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
